# The http.request_header / http.response_header http1 multi-buffers (header
# name+value pairs) populate line by line during the HEADERS progress. The
# marker headers arrive in the second segment of each side: on the first
# segment the multi-buffers do not yet contain them, so the no-match there is
# PROVISIONAL (the multi-buffers are streaming) and must not be converted to
# CANT_MATCH.
#
# * flows A1/A2 (49350-49351): "X-Marker: valA" (request) and
#   "X-RespMark: valA" (response); both keywords match on the second
#   segment and the flows are accepted.
# * flow B (49352): "valB" on both sides; no keyword matches; the toserver
#   side is dropped once (the toclient side is masked by the flow drop).
#
# Expected: exactly 1 `firewall default app policy` drop (flow B).
# allow session setup
accept:hook tcp:all $HOME_NET any <> $EXTERNAL_NET any (flow:not_established; sid:1021;)
accept:hook tcp:all $HOME_NET any <> $EXTERNAL_NET any (flow:established; sid:1022;)

accept:flow,alert http1:<request_headers $HOME_NET any -> $EXTERNAL_NET any (http.request_header; content:"X-Marker: valA"; sid:211;)
accept:flow,alert http1:<response_headers $EXTERNAL_NET any -> $HOME_NET any (http.response_header; content:"X-RespMark: valA"; sid:212;)
